id:                     E2169
trigger_tool:           autoreconf|aclocal|automake|perl
phase:                  configuration
error_signature:        \.aclocal-real: No such file or directory|Cwd\.c: loadable library and perl binaries are mismatched|ac-config-macro-dirs\.m4: no such file or directory
severity:               3
category:               autotools|perl-abi|conan-build-tools|ohos
match_keywords:         aclocal-real, automake-real, PERL5LIB, automake-acdir, Cwd.c, HarmonyOS
title:                  Distinguish a missing Automake real script from its missing shebang interpreter before repairing the build
root_cause:             On HarmonyOS PC, the published Automake package contained .aclocal-real, but its shebang named absent /data/service/hnp/bin/perl; the wrapper therefore reported the real script as No such file or directory even though it existed. After bypassing that ambiguity, inherited Perl library paths could load an incompatible Cwd binary module, and Automake's Perl module directory still had to be distinguished from its aclocal macro directory.
affected_scope:         Autotools/Conan builds on HarmonyOS PC where the published Automake package contains .aclocal-real and .automake-real plus share/automake-<version>, share/aclocal-<version>, and share/aclocal directories.
verification_cmd:       First test -f <automake-bin>/.aclocal-real and test -e <shebang-interpreter> separately; inspect the shebang with head -n 1; invoke the real scripts with native perl; run autoreconf -fi and conan create with an installed-package consumer on the target.
rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           invoke-published-automake-real-scripts
rec_description:        In the recipe's build environment, use the native Perl executable for ACLOCAL and AUTOMAKE, set PERL to that interpreter, limit PERL5LIB to the Automake package's pure-Perl module directory, pass share/aclocal-<version> to --automake-acdir and share/automake-<version> to --libdir, then run autoreconf -fi. Preserve the published dependency package.
rec_command:            PERL=<native-perl> PERL5LIB=<automake-share>/automake-<version> ACLOCAL='<native-perl> <automake-bin>/.aclocal-real --automake-acdir=<automake-share>/aclocal-<version> --system-acdir=<automake-share>/aclocal' AUTOMAKE='<native-perl> <automake-bin>/.automake-real --libdir=<automake-share>/automake-<version>' autoreconf -fi
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               conan-build-command-environment
fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      rebuild-automake-for-target
fallback_description:   If the package lacks the real scripts or its layout differs, rebuild/publish a corrected Automake package, or use a release tarball with compatible generated files after confirming that regeneration is unnecessary.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          manual
forbid_1_pattern:       PERL5LIB=.*site_perl.*Cwd|PERL5LIB=.*lib/5\.
forbid_1_reason:        An unrelated packaged Perl's binary Cwd module may not match the native interpreter ABI.
forbid_1_consequence:   autoreconf exits with a Perl handshake-key mismatch before configuration.
forbid_2_pattern:       --automake-acdir=.*/share/automake-
forbid_2_reason:        --automake-acdir expects the aclocal macro directory, not Automake's Perl module directory.
forbid_2_consequence:   aclocal/autom4te cannot find internal/ac-config-macro-dirs.m4.
principles:             P014
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             [E037,E049,E116]
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []
